[TEXT] **Root cause found!** The iptables FORWARD chain on router6 has explicit DROP rules for all traffic ingressing on **eth2** (the link toward router3/rest-of-network):

```
ACCEPT  tcp  in=eth2  src=172.16.10.0/24  dst=172.18.51.1  dport=80
DROP    tcp  in=eth2  any→any
DROP    udp  in=eth2  any→any
DROP    icmp in=eth2  any→any   ← 22 packets/1848 bytes already dropped (our pings!)
```

Return traffic (replies from pc4, pc11, etc.) arrives on eth2 and must be forwarded to eth0/eth1 — these DROP rules kill every reply. Forward probes from pc15/laptop4 egress on eth2 (not blocked), but their **replies** enter on eth2 and get dropped. Router6 itself can ping pc4 because its own traffic hits the INPUT chain, not FORWARD.

